  "comments": [
    {
      "author": "ZenoPageBuilder",
      "text": "Hello  @aspanner1     \n It happened because the missing product info is malformed or in an invalid format. I think you should check the missing ones and manually create them in Shopify Admin.",
      "at": "2023-09-07T02:52:44.000Z",
      "url": "https://community.shopify.com/t/shopify-missing-products-from-uploaded-csv/248282/2"
    },
    {
      "author": "aspanner1",
      "text": "Could you look at the attached file and let me know how they are malformed \nor invalid? I looked carefully and couldn’t find any difference. Thanks.",
      "at": "2023-09-07T02:54:22.000Z",
      "url": "https://community.shopify.com/t/shopify-missing-products-from-uploaded-csv/248282/3"
    },
    {
      "author": "Tubingbing",
      "text": "Hi  @aspanner1  — I found your post where Shopify’s error email pointed at specific lines, yet the products on those lines imported fine while your best-selling Meyer Lemon Olive Oil silently went missing. \n I’m honest upfront: I’m researching before building anything. I have an idea for a small CSV-checking tool for Shopify merchants, but there is no product yet — nothing to buy, and I’m not selling anything. \n Would you be open to a 15-minute chat about how you import / update products, and the last time a CSV import went wrong? I just want to learn what’s actually painful, so I don’t build the wrong thing. \n Happy to work around your timezone, voice or text — whichever is easier. And if it’s useful, I can share a short summary of what I hear from other merchants (anonymised) once I’ve done a few chats. \n If not, no worries at all — thanks for reading.",
      "at": "2026-10-24T10:24:44.480Z",
      "url": "https://community.shopify.com/t/shopify-missing-products-from-uploaded-csv/248282/4"
    },
    {
      "author": "Muhammad_Saleem_Baba",
      "text": "The two errors are different problems, and the missing product is almost certainly a third one. Shopify only rejects the rows it names, so a product that is not named in the email was not rejected. It was merged, skipped, or filed somewhere you are not looking. \n 1. Title is too long (lines 185-196): Shopify titles are capped at 255 characters. Shorten the Title on those rows to under 255 characters. Do not just move the extra text to the description, because the Title column itself is what is validated. Then re-import only those rows. \n 2. The variant ‘Sampler (30 mL)’ already exists (lines 1110-1117): that option combination already exists under the same Handle, either in the store or twice in your file. Two rows with the same Handle and the same Option1, Option2 and Option3 values are the same variant to Shopify. Find the duplicate Sampler (30 mL) rows for that Handle, keep one, and give the other a different option value or delete it. If you are updating an existing product, make sure the Handle matches exactly, including case and hyphens, and tick Overwrite products with matching handles on import. Otherwise Shopify will not update the existing variant. \n 3. For Meyer Lemon Olive Oil, check these in order before re-importing: search Products by its exact Handle and by its SKU, not just by title; check Drafts and Archived products; and check whether its variants were attached to another product with the same or a very similar Handle. A common cause here is a Handle that repeats or changes slightly between rows, so the rows get merged into a different product instead of creating the product you expect. Also check Status. A row with Status set to draft will import but will not show on the storefront. And check that the first row for that product has a Title, a Handle, and a Variant Price in plain decimal form, for example 12.99, with no currency symbol. \n Fix the title and the duplicate variant, then import a small test file containing only the Meyer Lemon rows, with Overwrite checked, and check the import email again. It will name any rows that still fail, line by line.",
      "at": "2026-11-02T23:02:19.458Z",
      "url": "https://community.shopify.com/t/shopify-missing-products-from-uploaded-csv/248282/5"
    }
  ],
